The program's own lasting switch for every picture is the stereo layer's "Enable 3D" (Stereo::Enable3DAction), in the
same words as every program on the layer, at the top of the 3D menu of the album preview, the light table, the editor
and the slide show, in place of a second entry called "Not 3D" (ORDER 551c). Off, every picture is shown flat, and it
stays off after a restart as before (the settings' View is 3); "Not 3D" for one file stays in the layer's menu.
Alt+Shift+N switches it; choosing Stereo, Left eye only or Right eye only shows the pictures in 3D again. The slide
show now starts with the program's lasting view, as the other picture areas do.

A stored 3D choice that cannot follow a file digiKam itself renamed or moved (the per-file store cannot be written) is
told to the person, from the main thread whatever thread the job ran in, one window for a burst of files; before, it
was only written to the log. A folder digiKam moves to another device, by a copy and a removal, now carries the
choices of its files too.

The eleven sentences the 3D menu keeps and the new one are in Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, French, German, Spanish,
Japanese, Korean and Chinese (../../translations/digikam-stereo3d.po.patch, last in the series); they were English in
every language since +stereo3d1. Enable 3D and the per-file entries are the layer's and come from its catalogues.

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.19.2.
